abstract: |
  Tobramycin is a WHO essential aminoglycoside restricted to intravenous
  and inhaled routes (oral F ≈ 1–2%). This repository resolves its BCS
  classification as Class III (high solubility 94–100 mg/mL, low permeability
  Papp < 1×10⁻⁶ cm/s), builds a validated whole-body PBPK model in PK-Sim
  from the OSP amikacin model (gate 6/6 PASS, 577.5 mg, 30-min infusion),
  calibrates transcellular intestinal permeability to the clinical baseline
  (Pint0 3×10⁻⁹ dm/min → F0 1.75%), and optimizes a 10-dimensional formulation
  design space (HIP complex, SEDDS, nanoparticles, permeation enhancers,
  coatings, dose) with NSGA-II inside the PK-Sim loop under a cited-bounded
  enhancement model (cap ×126.3 at logP +1.6, Asad et al. 2023). Winner
  TOBP-001 ×125, 999.8 mg QD, F96 97.1%, Cmax/MIC 31.2, AUC/MIC 172;
  legacy re-evaluated A ×73.9, 550.6 mg QD, AUC/MIC 87.3; requirement map
  shows ×33 already attains AUC≥80 at 993 mg.

